  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "So we all have the ability to choose who's avatars we can see so why not add the ability for us to choose who can see our avatar like a privacy feature, this would primarily be used to combat random strangers joining a lobby and ripping all avatars in the lobby then just leaving\n\nBecause if they can't see your avatar then they can't rip it\n\nI mainly suggested this idea because I don't use my main avatar in public worlds anymore because I'm scared of it getting stolen by some random stranger who joins the world for a minute rips all the avatars and leaves (Yes this has actually happened to me many times)\n\nAnd yes Easy Anti Cheat is being bypassed, It was supposed to stop stuff like avatar ripping however it's just made it worse because people can no longer use modded clients to prevent ripping so they are completely defenseless against it\n\nMy avatar is literally who I am so this feature would help me and probably many many other avatar creators a lot\n\nIt may not stop avatar ripping completely but at least you'll have interacted with the person who's ripped your avatar instead of never meeting them\n\nPlease consider this idea because I think it would work really well and you could even have fallback avatars show for people that aren't allowed to see your avatar\n\nUpvote this post if you think this is a good idea, Thank you for your time and have a lovely day and or night",
